  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Find the point of intersection of the parabola ${y}^{2}-x+10y+21=0$ with the $x$-axis.",
  "worked_solution": "When the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we set $y=0$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-x+10y+21 & =0 \\\\ (0)^{2}-x+10(0)+21 & =0 \\\\ -x+21 & =0 \\\\ x & =21\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parabola intersects the $x$-axis at $(21,0).$",
